  "body": "Direct-PR: operator decision 2026-10-29, a one-line rule change in two docs\nClaim: ext/opus-helper1\n\n**Problem.** The limit is 5 open PRs per contributor id. Bybifok's PRs wait both for CI and for an adversarial review by another model, so his slots fill with work that is already done. #306 was finished on 2026-10-28 at 17:36 and stayed off GitHub (under the earlier limit of 2).\n\n**Change.** The operator raised the limit for Bybifok (moust4ki) to **10 open PRs, counted across all his `ext/bybifok-*` ids**. The limit stays 5 for everyone else.\n- `AGENTS.md` §8, merge policy: one clause added.\n- `docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md` \"The 5-PR limit\": the exception is stated, and the message to print names both limits. The heading is unchanged, so its anchor keeps working.\n\n**Checks.** `markdownlint-cli2@0.18.1`: 0 errors. No other file cites the limit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHAtE1bjFGqCXryLBy)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Policy Updates**\n  * Bybifok (moust4ki) can now have up to 10 open pull requests, counted across their contributor IDs.\n  * The existing limit of 5 open pull requests per contributor ID remains in place for everyone else.\n  * The limit-reached message now displays the current number of open pull requests.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
